  title: 'Hainanese Immigrants 19th Century '
  info: 'Hainanese immigrants, initially employed as cooks and domestic helpers in
    colonial households, introduced culinary staples such as kaya toast and chicken
    rice. Over time, they transitioned to running coffee shops and food stalls, embedding
    their unique flavors into Singapore''s multicultural cuisine.  '
